>> title: Chicken Thighs, Air Fryer
>> category: Fried & Crispy
>> tags: chicken, thighs, air fryer, basket, weeknight, one thing to wash
>> counters: The Air Fryer & the Pot
>> aka: air fryer chicken thighs, basket chicken thighs, crispy skin chicken thighs, bone-in air fryer chicken
>> servings: 4
>> time: 40 min
>> slack: narrow — the meat is forgiving well past 74°C and the skin is not; five minutes after it crisps it goes from crackling to leather
>> washing-up: the basket

>> step: Written for a preheated 5.7 L basket. From cold, add three minutes. A 3.5 L basket is two batches, not more minutes.
The seasoning goes on in the basket, so the basket is the only thing.

>> step: rub them in the basket itself, skin side up
Rub @bone-in skin-on chicken thighs{4}(about 1.5 lb / 700 g; patted dry) in a preheated #air fryer basket{} with @olive oil{2%tsp}, @kosher salt{2%tsp}, @smoked paprika{1%tsp}, @garlic powder{1%tsp}, @black pepper{1/2%tsp}.

>> step: roast in the basket 190°C (375°F), 22–25 min, one layer
Roast @&(~1)rubbed thighs{} skin side up at 190°C (375°F) for ~air fry{23%min}, one layer, and do not turn them.

>> step: probe the thickest part — 74°C (165°F), and that number is not a range
Probe @&(~1)thighs{} at the thickest part, off the bone.

>> step: rest 5 min, then squeeze the lemon over
Rest @&(~1)thighs{} for ~rest{5%min}, then squeeze @lemon{1/2}(cut in wedges) over them.
